<!--CLI Documentation — InitCommand
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.InitCommand-->
<clidoc:InitCommand xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    machineblocks init specification
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Syntax:
        machineblocks init <package-fqn> [--src dir] [--no-install]

        Scaffolds a BlockML project by calling initProject from @blockml/cli
        with noInstall true, then records the MachineBlocks profile. It does not
        spawn blockml init. The profile is recorded before npm install so the
        installed corpus is the project this command just wrote.
        PACKAGE-FQN is a dotted package identifier, not ….Library. A bml segment
        after the domain is recommended. Compile maps a bml segment to scad.
        --src changes the source directory (default blocks).
        Preflight runs inside that initProject call, before any write, including
        the profile. --no-install does not skip it. A project is BlockML when
        package.json has a blockml key. An unreadable package.json fails
        preflight with exit 2 and writes nothing. When the key is present,
        AGENTS.md stays and generation overwrites it after npm install. When
        the key is absent, an existing AGENTS.md is renamed to
        AGENTS.md.pre-blockml. If that backup already exists, preflight exits 2
        and writes nothing.
        By default, after the profile is recorded, npm install runs and then
        GenerateAgentsMd overwrites AGENTS.md, by the same step as initProject.
        --no-install skips both.
        At least one section or rule overwrites AGENTS.md. No AgentInstructions
        content leaves the file unwritten and prints
        "No AgentInstructions blocks found."; the init exit code stays 0.
        The next-step line from the earlier initProject pass is dropped,
        because install already ran.
        With --no-install, npm install and AGENTS.md generation are skipped.
        When AGENTS.md is missing, initProject's next line remains:
        npm install && npx blockml agents-md generate. When AGENTS.md is
        already present, the next line is npm install && npx blockml validate.
        CLAUDE.md (@AGENTS.md) is written by initProject when missing.
        The profile adds @machineblocks/cli to devDependencies when that package
        is absent from dependencies and devDependencies. The range is the caret
        range of this host. An existing dependencies entry stays put.
        The project Library.bml gains a dependencies composition child
        com.machineblocks.bml.Library. An existing child is left in place.
        Existing BML files and CLAUDE.md are not replaced. AGENTS.md is the
        generated artifact described above.
        A package FQN without a bml segment still exits 0 and warns:
        Package FQN has no bml segment. Compile maps a bml segment to scad.
        Exit codes match initProject: 0 success, 1 write, rename, or install
        failure, 2 usage, an invalid package FQN, or a failed preflight.

    Printed help:
    Usage: machineblocks init <package-fqn> [--src dir] [--no-install]
           machineblocks init --help

    When: turn a directory into a MachineBlocks project. Scaffolds a BlockML project,
    then records the MachineBlocks profile.

    PACKAGE-FQN is a dotted package identifier (not …Library). A bml segment after
    the domain is recommended. Compile maps a bml segment to scad.
    A package FQN without a bml segment still exits 0 and warns.
    Does not spawn blockml init. Calls initProject from @blockml/cli with noInstall
    true, then records the profile before npm install.

    Preflight runs before any write and checks conditions. --no-install does not skip it.
    A project is BlockML when package.json has a blockml key. Then AGENTS.md
    stays, and agents-md generate overwrites it after npm install.
    Otherwise an existing AGENTS.md is renamed to AGENTS.md.pre-blockml.
    Does not overwrite existing BML files or CLAUDE.md.

    The profile adds @machineblocks/cli to devDependencies when that package is
    absent from dependencies and devDependencies. The range is the caret range of
    this host. An existing dependencies entry stays put.
    The project Library.bml gains com.machineblocks.bml.Library.
    CLAUDE.md (@AGENTS.md) is written when missing.

    Runs npm install, then generates AGENTS.md, unless --no-install is passed.
    --no-install skips npm install and AGENTS.md generation. It does not skip preflight.
    AGENTS.md is overwritten when at least one section or rule is found.
    When no AgentInstructions content is found, AGENTS.md is left unwritten.
    The next-step line from the earlier initProject pass is dropped when install runs.
    With --no-install and no AGENTS.md, that next step remains:
    npm install && npx blockml agents-md generate.

    Flags:
      --src dir       source directory (default blocks)
      --no-install    skip npm install and AGENTS.md generation

    Exit codes match initProject: 0 success, 1 write, rename, or install failure,
    2 usage, an invalid package FQN, or a failed preflight.

    Related: validate, compile. agents-md and new stay on blockml.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidoc:Configuration" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="clidoc:Commands" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</clidoc:InitCommand>
